{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789341698,"nonce":"2LC+lgwVb8LlZOyz5BJiVXXhmR0=","title":"A send from compiled code reads its thread state once, and a host method is cached","message":"A `wren_call_N` send from Cranelift code cost fifteen thread-local reads on\nmacOS, where each is an out-of-line `_tlv_get_addr`: the entry counter read\nthe VM through the JIT context, the roots were pushed and read back one by\none, the frame stack was its own thread-local, the frameless pass and\n`dispatch_call_rooted` each looked the VM up again, and the call-site IC\nread the context once more. A host method (`Method::Host`, from 1b42702)\nthen found by the method cache in the frameless pass was dropped and looked\nup a second time in `dispatch_call_rooted`, and it had no IC kind, so an\ninline-IC site compiled by the `mod.rs` backend always took the slow path\nfor it.\n\nMeasured with caribou's interop bench (Wren calling a Haxe static through a\nhost method, ns per call, median of 5 runs of 200k): 52.5 before, 46.9 with\nthe frame stack folded into `JitThread` and the state read once per send,\n42 once the frameless pass runs a host method it found without a second\nlookup. Ash's sampler put `wren_call_1_inner` plus `dispatch_call_rooted`\nplus `dispatch_method` at 25% of the call and `_tlv_get_addr` at 16%\nbefore; after, `wren_call_1_inner` alone is 12% and the thread-local reads\n5% (one for the JIT state, one in the caller's adapter).\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- `JitThread` gains `frames` (the frame stack for GC walking) and\n  `disabled` (was `JIT_DISABLED`, which nothing ever set). `push_jit_frame`,\n  `pop_jit_frame`, `jit_frame_entries` and `jit_disabled` keep their\n  signatures and go through `jit_state()`.\n- One generic `wren_call_inner\u003cM\u003e` behind `wren_call_0..4_inner` and\n  `wren_call_n_inner`: fetches the JIT state once, roots the words, takes\n  the VM from the state, and threads both through\n  `try_dispatch_call_noframe_fast(vm, ..)`, `dispatch_call_rooted(vm, j, ..)`\n  and `current_jit_callsite_ic(vm, j, ..)`. `dispatch_call` and `vm_ref`\n  are the wrappers that still look the state up, for their other callers.\n- The frameless pass answers `Frameless::Host(fn, ctx)` for a host method\n  the cache resolves; the send pushes its frame and calls it there.\n- IC kind 8 is a host method: `closure` holds the fn, `func_id` the\n  context word. `populate_callsite_ic` fills it, `try_dispatch_callsite_ic`\n  runs it, and the `mod.rs` inline IC dispatches it through\n  `wren_ic_host_0..3(fn, ctx, recv, args..)`, naked on aarch64 to capture\n  the frame pointer as the native trampolines do. The Cranelift backend\n  encodes an IC index only under `WLIFT_ENABLE_JIT_CALLSITE_IC`, so on that\n  tier the win comes from the frameless pass, not the IC.\n- `call_found_closure` reads `disabled` from the state it already holds\n  and saves and restores only the context fields it writes; a cross-module\n  call restores the rest itself.\n\nNot done: a per-site cache for host methods on the Cranelift tier (the IC\nindex is off by default there), and the method cache probe itself, which\nis now the send's only lookup.","files":null}]}